#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Copyright 2026 Theorem Labs, PBC
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""Decide what enroll-dispatch.yml does after a run of Review, Validate, Terms, Tests, Maintainer confirmed or
Enrollment merged completes.

    GH_TOKEN=... REPO=theorem-labs/oss-verify RUN_ID=<run> RUN_EVENT=<event> HEAD_SHA=<commit> \
      .github/scripts/enroll-dispatch

RUN_ID, RUN_EVENT and HEAD_SHA are the completed run's. It reads GitHub's API only, with a read-only token: nothing of
the pull request is checked out or run. It writes nine lines to $GITHUB_OUTPUT (and to standard output): decision,
label, pr, project and sha; one line, reason, that says why; and review_passed, review_passed_at and label_at, which
say what happens to the label review-passed (below). A dispatch for a merge writes one more, merged=true, which
enroll-dispatch.yml adds to the event's client_payload. The decision is:

  dispatch  the workflow sends the event enrollment-checked for pr, project and sha
  label     the workflow puts `label` on the pull request, and sends nothing:
              size-review      a plain binary is larger than SIZE_LIMIT, or its size could not be read (a binary the
                               loader maps no executable byte of is one)
              language-paused  the project's language is one whose projects are paused for now
              name-review      the project's name has a dot, which the statements repository's names cannot have
              maintainer-review  the pull request's author is not shown to maintain the repository that `repo`
                               names, by triage.py's maintainer check (the author, not primary_contact), or that
                               repository is not on github.com, or the check could not read it
                               (not when someone other than the author who can label, a member of theorem-labs
                               or one of its Apps, put maintainer-confirmed on after the head commit was pushed:
                               then the check is skipped)
  none      anything else; `reason` says what. Among them: the newest check run Enrollment review of the oss-verify
            App (REVIEW_APP) at the commit for the pull request (its external_id is the pull request's number) is not
            success, or there is none (not yet reviewed); a project.yaml whose language cannot be read; a steering file
            that no person approved (below). review.yml's comment job writes that check run with the review comment,
            and the completion of that Review run runs this again. A check run of another pull request at the same
            commit is not counted.

Which commit, whose pull request, and whose record. A run of a pull request (pull_request, or pull_request_target,
which the workflows ran on before the move below) is about its head commit, and about the head it came from (the
repository and branch of that run). A Review run (REVIEW_WORKFLOW) runs on main, so its own head commit and head name
no pull request:

  - A Review run after a Build run (workflow_run, title "Review of run <id>") is about the head commit and the head of
    the run that its title names, which must be a run of build.yaml on pull_request. review.yml's comment job writes
    the check run Enrollment review in the Review run, so the Review run's completion, not the Build run's, has this
    decide.
  - A Review run started by hand on main (gh workflow run review.yml -f pr=<n>, title "Pull request <n>") is about the
    head commit and the head of pull request <n>. That is how a maintainer has this look again at a pull request.

Any other run, but a merge's (below), is none. Among them: a Review run whose title names a Triage run or no run, a
Review run of an issue ("Issue <n>") or of a measurement ("Measure the screen"), and a run by hand of another file.

A merge. A run of Enrollment merged (MERGED_WORKFLOW) is about the pull request its title names ("merged #<n>"), and
is decided by decide_merged. The run is on pull_request (the merge commit's copy of the file, which the pull request
can change: so the run must be from that pull request's head repository and branch, at its head commit or its merge
commit), on pull_request_target (the base branch's copy, which is main's for a pull request into main, before the
move), or a replay by hand on main (gh workflow run enroll-merged.yml -f pr=<n>). That pull request must be merged into
main and its files all under one projects/<name>/; every required check must have passed at its head commit, bound as
below to the head it came from; and the record (below) must be of that commit, pull request and project. A pull
request that changes a steering file must also have a person's approval of that commit (below). Then the size line, a
paused language and the name rule label as above, and else the head commit is sent, with merged=true. The review (the
check run Enrollment review) and the maintainer check (maintainer-review) are not asked: the person who merged decided
them. A run that did not succeed (its job runs for a merge or a replay alone), of another file, event or branch, or
whose title names no pull request, is none. So is a run on pull_request from another head or commit: a later pull
request from the same branch, whose own run names an older merged one, sends nothing. A merge after the statements
started is sent too: the statements repository skips a commit whose facts it made or whose build started in the last
24 hours.

Every required check is bound to its source: each check of REQUIRED_SOURCES, and any other the ruleset of main
requires (rules/branches/main), must have passed at that commit in a run of the workflow file REQUIRED_SOURCES names,
on one of the events it names, whose head commit is that commit and whose head is that head; of those runs, the newest
decides. A check run of the same name from any other run (a run of another file or event, a run of another commit, a
second pull request at the same commit from another head) is not counted, and a required check with no entry in
REQUIRED_SOURCES or PULL_CHECKS is never passed. Each check of PULL_CHECKS (review, which review.yml's comment job
posts) must have passed at that commit in the newest check run of its name by the oss-verify App for that pull
request, as Enrollment review is read. build.yaml, validate.yaml and terms.yaml ran on pull_request_target, and they
run on pull_request after they moved to it (the move). A run on either event counts, so that the checks of a head that
ran before the move still count. A pull_request_target run ran the base branch's copy of the file. The bound checks
are of a pull request into main (open_at, and the base check of a merge), so for them that copy is main's. A
pull_request run runs the merge commit's copy, which a pull request that changes the file controls: the_project makes
every such pull request none, as it has a file outside one projects/<name>/. The record is the artifact
enrollment-record of the Build run whose project-builds check is the bound one, which build.yaml's record job wrote
from project-builds' outputs; every value of it is checked against its shape.

The pull request of any other run is the one the record names. It must be open, into main, from that head, with that
commit as its head commit, and its files must all be under one projects/<name>/, the record's project; it is read again
after its files, and a pull request whose head moved meanwhile is none (the run for the new head decides). A draft pull
request is none: build.yaml runs again on ready_for_review, and the Review run after that run decides for the pull
request once it is ready.

The steering-file gate. A steering file can change what a workflow runs, or what Claude Code loads in the review job
(steering.py lists them: each file under .github/, src/, infra/ and seeds/ among others, and files at any depth such as
projects/<name>/AGENTS.md). So when a file of the pull request (by its name or its
previous name) is a steering file, the run is none, for an open pull request and for a merge, unless a person approved
the commit (person_approval of .github/scripts/approval.py, which review-check reads too). With
that approval the run goes on, and its reason says who approved. A person approval is a review of the pull request in
state APPROVED, of that commit, by a user of type User who is not the pull request's author and whose collaborator
permission is admin or write. That user's newest review in state APPROVED, CHANGES_REQUESTED or DISMISSED must be that
approval. A read that fails gives no approval. A person approval starts no run: after a person approves such a head, a
re-run of the newest Enroll dispatch run of that head (gh run rerun <id>), or any later event, decides again.

A pull request that changes a project already enrolled is sent too: its facts are made again at the new commit.

The sizes are read from the ELF headers of the files the project's own build wrote, so a build that rewrites its
program headers can make them small. The statements repository measures its own build again. Its facts pull request
merges after its checks pass and an agent reviews it; no person reviews it.

The label review-passed says that an enrollment passed at its head commit: its statements were started, and Theorem
has no plan to merge or prove it now. enroll-dispatch.yml puts it on and takes it off, as review_passed says: on, off,
or empty for no change. review_passed_at is head for a change at a new head and for a renewal, closed for a close or a
merge, and else empty. label_at is the time of the newest labeled event that the decision judged, for a change at a
new head and for a renewal; the workflow takes the label off at a new head only when that event is still the newest.
For a renewal it takes it off before the send and puts it on again after (unless the newest removal since label_at is
a person's), so that a send that fails leaves it off. Events of its former name, passes-not-merging, count as its own.
The reason says why the label changes, or why it does not.

The run's pull request is the one the decision names; when a decision none names none (required checks not passed,
say), it is the pull request into main from the run's head at its commit, an open one before a closed one. When that
pull request is closed (merged or not) and carries the label, the run takes it off, whatever it decides and whatever
its head: so a later run (a label put on the closed pull request, a Review run started by hand) takes off what a run of
Enrollment merged that failed left. Else a run changes the label only when its commit is that pull request's head
commit and the pull request is open; a late run for an older head changes nothing, and nor does a none that binds no
head (no commit id, a run of another commit, another event). A run of maintainer-confirmed.yml for a label other than
maintainer-confirmed binds its head: it is the first run for a new head when that label is put on before any other
run completes, and it takes off a label older than that head. Then:

  The run passes: its decision is dispatch, which it gives only when the review's check run Enrollment review at the
  commit is success (an optional fail of F5 or F8 still gives success), and the pull request is an enrollment: its
  files are under one projects/<name>/ (the decision dispatch shows that).

  When the label is off, a run that passes puts it on when review.yml's rule for trusted accounts does not trust the
  author, with a clear answer (a read that fails is not one), unless an account other than the oss-verify App took
  it off that pull request before (an unlabeled event, at any time). When the label is on and older than the run's
  commit, a run that passes puts it on again, whoever the author is (the trust is not read), so that its labeled
  event is new and the label is for that commit (the workflow takes it off before the send and puts it on after);
  any other run takes it off. A label that is not older than the run's commit stays, whatever that run decides.

The label is for the head the pull request was at when its newest labeled event was made. Each labeled event starts a
run of maintainer-confirmed.yml (CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW, on pull_request, or on pull_request_target before the move) at
that head, by the account that put the label on, a few seconds after the event. The runs from the pull request's head
made by that account in the ten minutes after the event (CONFIRMED_WINDOW) give the commits the label may be for. When
they give exactly one, the label is for it, and older than the run's commit when it is another, unless that account
put another label on (any label) in those ten minutes: then the one run found may be that label's, at another head,
with the label's own run missing, and the head is ambiguous. When they give none (the run was deleted or made late, or
the event names no account), or more than one (that account put a label on at another head in those ten minutes), or
the head is ambiguous, the label is older than the run's commit: a true label may come off, and a false one never
stays. A run whose read of the pull request's events, or of those runs, fails changes nothing. A run of Enrollment
merged, a skipped one too, takes the label off the closed pull request its title names (merged or not) when it
carries it, whatever else it decides, and never puts it on.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import datetime
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import urllib.parse
from urllib.parse import quote

import yaml

# triage.py's maintainer check, the one the triage table shows as "Opened by an active maintainer". steering.py's list
# of steering files, for the steering-file gate. artifact.py's read of one file of a Build run's artifact for the record
# (read_member), the errors that this read does not catch (UNREADABLE), Api, the check of a whole number (whole), and
# the runs of a required check's workflow at a head (runs_at) and the one that gives the check (deciding_run).
# approval.py's person approval of a commit (person_approval), the one rule that review-check reads too, with the
# write access, the login's shape and the time that it reads.
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import steering  # noqa: E402
import triage  # noqa: E402
from approval import LOGIN, person_approval, time_of, write_access  # noqa: E402
from artifact import UNREADABLE, Api, deciding_run, read_member, runs_at, whole  # noqa: E402

# The size line for statements that start with no person's decision, "Up to 1 MB" of a plain binary
# (dispatch://OSSV-141/ask/7c73eb21), the README's "less than 1 MB of code": 1 MB is 1,000,000 bytes here. It is
# applied to the larger of the .text section's size and the bytes the loader maps executable, which renaming or
# resizing a section does not change (src/oss_verify/manifest.py, executable_bytes); the executable segments can hold
# read-only data too, so the measure errs toward a person's review, never away from it.
SIZE_LIMIT = 1_000_000
# Languages whose projects are paused for now. Go builds, but our tools write no theorem statements for it yet
# (docs/project-yaml.md, "language").
PAUSED_LANGUAGES = frozenset({"python", "go"})
# The events of a run of a pull request: pull_request, and pull_request_target, which build.yaml, validate.yaml,
# terms.yaml and maintainer-confirmed.yml ran on before the move. A pull_request_target run ran the base branch's copy
# of its file. The bound checks are of a pull request into main (open_at, and the base check of a merge), so for them
# that copy is main's, and a run of a head from before the move still counts.
PULL_EVENTS = frozenset({"pull_request", "pull_request_target"})
# The workflow file and the events each required check must come from. Each is required here whatever the ruleset
# says, and so is any other check the ruleset requires (which, with no source here, is never passed).
REQUIRED_SOURCES = {
    "project-builds": (".github/workflows/build.yaml", PULL_EVENTS),
    "enrollment": (".github/workflows/validate.yaml", PULL_EVENTS),
    "terms-accepted": (".github/workflows/terms.yaml", PULL_EVENTS),
    "tests": (".github/workflows/tests.yaml", frozenset({"pull_request"})),
}
# The checks that review.yml's comment job posts as the oss-verify App (REVIEW_APP) for one pull request, with the
# pull request's number as external_id (.github/scripts/review-check; R14 of dispatch://INFRA-5359/spec): each is
# bound to that App and that pull request, as REVIEW_CHECK is, not to a run (its details_url is the review comment's
# address). Each is required here whatever the ruleset says, as each of REQUIRED_SOURCES is (pull_checks).
PULL_CHECKS = ("review",)
# GitHub Actions, the app of every check run above. A theorem-labs/agent-infra change makes main's ruleset require the
# four from the oss-verify App, whose copy of each .github/workflows/required-checks.yml posts after the run ends. This
# script reads GitHub Actions' own check run of each instead, whatever App the ruleset names (required_checks).
ACTIONS_APP = 15368
BUILD_WORKFLOW = ".github/workflows/build.yaml"
RECORD_ARTIFACT = "enrollment-record"
RECORD_SCHEMA = "oss-verify enrollment record v1"
# The review's verdict: the check run REVIEW_CHECK that review.yml's comment job writes on the reviewed commit with the
# review comment, as the oss-verify App (REVIEW_APP; gh api apps/oss-verify), with the pull request's number as its
# external_id. A check run of the same name from any other App, or of another pull request at the same commit, is not
# counted. Only its conclusion success starts statements; a pull request with no such check run at the commit is
# NOT_REVIEWED.
REVIEW_CHECK = "Enrollment review"
REVIEW_APP = 5447700
NOT_REVIEWED = "not yet reviewed"
# Review: its comment job writes REVIEW_CHECK, and its completion runs this. A run on workflow_run, and a run by hand on
# main, is main's copy. Its title (review.yml's run-name) names what it reviewed: the run after which it ran, or the
# pull request that a run by hand names.
REVIEW_WORKFLOW = ".github/workflows/review.yml"
REVIEW_RUN_TITLE = re.compile(r"Review of run ([1-9][0-9]*)")
REVIEW_PULL_TITLE = re.compile(r"Pull request ([1-9][0-9]*)")
# The label that someone other than the author, who can label (a member of theorem-labs, or one of its Apps), puts on an enrollment whose author the maintainer check does not show (a
# pull request that our bot opened at a maintainer's request, for one): with it, the check is skipped. Putting it on
# runs .github/workflows/maintainer-confirmed.yml, whose completion runs this again.
CONFIRMED_LABEL = "maintainer-confirmed"
CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW = ".github/workflows/maintainer-confirmed.yml"
# Every labeled event, of any label, starts a run of CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW at the pull request's head of that moment, a
# few seconds after it. A run made later than this after a label's newest labeled event is not counted as its own.
CONFIRMED_WINDOW = datetime.timedelta(minutes=10)
# The workflow whose run says that a pull request was closed, and, in its title, which: its job runs for a merge (or a
# replay of one by hand) alone. Its completion runs this, which sends a merged enrollment (decide_merged).
MERGED_WORKFLOW = ".github/workflows/enroll-merged.yml"
MERGED_TITLE = re.compile(r"merged #([1-9][0-9]*)")
DEFAULT_BRANCH = "main"
# The API lists at most 3,000 files of a pull request; above that, the list is not the whole change.
MAX_LISTED_FILES = 3000
MAX_ARTIFACT_BYTES = 1 << 20
MAX_PROJECT_YAML_BYTES = 256 * 1024
# A project's directory name, as oss-verify validate's NAME takes it, and the statements repository's project names,
# which have no dot.
NAME = re.compile(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,62}")
STATEMENTS_NAME = re.compile(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,62}")
SHA = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{40}")
# The label that says an enrollment passed at its head commit: its checks and its review passed, its statements were
# started, and Theorem has no plan to merge or prove it now. The events of a pull request labelled before the label
# was renamed give its former name, so both names count in them.
REVIEW_PASSED = "review-passed"
REVIEW_PASSED_NAMES = frozenset({REVIEW_PASSED, "passes-not-merging"})
# The oss-verify App, whose token enroll-dispatch.yml writes the label with. A removal by any other account is a
# person's, and the label does not go on again.
APP_LOGIN = "oss-verify[bot]"
# The checkout this script is in: review.yml there holds WRITER_BOTS.
CHECKOUT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))))


def outcome(decision: str, reason: str, pr: int | None = None, project: str = "", sha: str = "",
            label: str = "") -> dict:
    return {"decision": decision, "label": label, "pr": "" if pr is None else str(pr), "project": project,
            "sha": sha, "reason": " ".join(reason.split()), "review_passed": "", "review_passed_at": "", "label_at": ""}


def run_id_of(repo: str, url: object) -> int | None:
    """The Actions run a check run's details_url names, if it is a run of this repository."""
    m = re.fullmatch(r"https://github\.com/%s/actions/runs/([0-9]+)/job/[0-9]+" % re.escape(repo), str(url or ""))
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None


class Runs:
    """This repository's Actions runs, each read once."""

    def __init__(self, api: Api, repo: str):
        self.api, self.repo, self.seen = api, repo, {}

    def get(self, run_id: int) -> dict:
        if run_id not in self.seen:
            self.seen[run_id] = self.api.get(f"repos/{self.repo}/actions/runs/{run_id}")
        return self.seen[run_id]


def required_checks(api: Api, repo: str) -> list[tuple[str, int | None]]:
    """(context, integration id) of every status check the default branch's rules require, and every check of
    REQUIRED_SOURCES whether the rules list it or not: a ruleset that is off, or edited, lowers no bar here. A check of
    REQUIRED_SOURCES is read from GitHub Actions whatever App the rules name for it. bound_checks binds that check run to
    the run of its own workflow file, event and head, which is all that the oss-verify App's copy of it says
    (.github/workflows/required-checks.yml), and the App posts its copy only after the run ends: this script, which
    starts when the run ends, would not find the App's copy yet, and no later event would run it again."""
    out: dict[str, int | None] = {context: ACTIONS_APP for context in REQUIRED_SOURCES}
    out.update({context: REVIEW_APP for context in PULL_CHECKS})
    for rule in api.get(f"repos/{repo}/rules/branches/{DEFAULT_BRANCH}"):
        if rule.get("type") == "required_status_checks":
            for check in (rule.get("parameters") or {}).get("required_status_checks") or []:
                if check["context"] not in REQUIRED_SOURCES and check["context"] not in PULL_CHECKS:
                    out[check["context"]] = check.get("integration_id") or out.get(check["context"])
    return sorted(out.items())


def head_of(run: dict) -> tuple[object, object]:
    """The repository and branch a run's pull request came from."""
    return (run.get("head_repository") or {}).get("full_name"), run.get("head_branch")


def head_of_pull(pull: dict) -> tuple[object, object]:
    """The repository and branch a pull request comes from."""
    at = pull.get("head") or {}
    return (at.get("repo") or {}).get("full_name"), at.get("ref")


def bound_checks(api: Api, repo: str, sha: str, head: tuple, before: str | None = None) -> tuple[list[str], int | None]:
    """The required checks that have not passed at `sha` from their bound source, and the Actions run of the bound
    project-builds check (None if it has not passed). A check counts only from one run of its workflow file, on one of
    its events, at `sha`, of the pull request whose head is `head` (repository, branch): another pull request at the
    same commit from another head neither blocks this one nor speaks for it. A pull request from the same head (the same
    branch into another base) has the same runs. Of the runs GitHub lists, whether or not a run's job has started, the
    one that deciding_run of artifact.py takes decides for both, as it does for required-check's copy of the check: a
    job can start, and get its check run's id, in another order than the runs. Within that run, the newest check run of
    the name, its latest attempt's, decides; a run with none has not passed.

    `before` is a merged pull request's merged_at (decide_merged): only the runs created at or before the merge decide,
    because they are the runs the merge was made on. An edit of a merged pull request's description starts a Terms run
    of its own, which fails once the branch is gone (its checkout has no merge commit), and without `before` that run
    would hold an enrollment that every check passed for."""
    check_runs = [c for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}/check-runs?filter=all&per_page=100")
                  for c in page.get("check_runs") or []]
    waiting, build_run = [], None
    for context, app in required_checks(api, repo):
        if context in PULL_CHECKS:
            continue   # bound to a pull request, which pull_checks reads once the pull request is known
        source = REQUIRED_SOURCES.get(context)
        if source is None:
            waiting.append(f"{context} (no known source)")
            continue
        run = deciding_run([r for event in sorted(source[1])
                            for r in runs_at(api, repo, source[0], event, sha, head, before)])
        if run is None:
            waiting.append(f"{context} (not run by {source[0]} on {' or '.join(sorted(source[1]))})")
            continue
        check = max((c for c in check_runs if c.get("name") == context
                     and (app is None or (c.get("app") or {}).get("id") == app)
                     and run_id_of(repo, c.get("details_url")) == run["id"]), key=lambda c: c["id"], default=None)
        if check is None:
            waiting.append(f"{context} (no check run of run {run['id']})")
        elif check.get("status") != "completed" or check.get("conclusion") != "success":
            waiting.append(f"{context} ({check.get('conclusion') or check.get('status')})")
        elif context == "project-builds":
            build_run = run["id"]
    return waiting, build_run


def pull_checks(api: Api, repo: str, sha: str, number: int) -> list[str]:
    """Each check of PULL_CHECKS that has not passed at `sha` for pull request `number`, with why: the newest check run
    of that name by REVIEW_APP at `sha` whose external_id is `number` decides, as review_conclusion reads REVIEW_CHECK.
    A check run of that name from another App, or of another pull request at the same commit, is not counted."""
    check_runs = [c for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}/check-runs?filter=all&per_page=100")
                  for c in page.get("check_runs") or []]
    waiting = []
    for name in PULL_CHECKS:
        found = [c for c in check_runs if c.get("name") == name and (c.get("app") or {}).get("id") == REVIEW_APP
                 and c.get("external_id") == str(number)]
        if not found:
            waiting.append(f"{name} (not posted by the oss-verify App for pull request {number})")
            continue
        newest = max(found, key=lambda c: c["id"])
        if newest.get("status") != "completed" or newest.get("conclusion") != "success":
            waiting.append(f"{name} ({newest.get('conclusion') or newest.get('status')})")
    return waiting


def build_record(api: Api, repo: str, run_id: int) -> tuple[dict | None, str]:
    """The record build.yaml's record job uploaded in this run: the JSON of record.json, the one file of its artifact
    RECORD_ARTIFACT; or None and why not. read_member reads it, with the limit MAX_ARTIFACT_BYTES, and gives None and
    why for each artifact it refuses (an encrypted record.json among them). An exception of UNREADABLE (artifact.py)
    gives None and the error too: a zip or a record.json that zipfile cannot read, and a record.json that is not JSON
    (ValueError). A call of gh that fails raises subprocess.CalledProcessError."""
    try:
        data, why = read_member(api, repo, run_id, RECORD_ARTIFACT, "record.json", MAX_ARTIFACT_BYTES)
        return (None, why) if data is None else (json.loads(data), "")
    except UNREADABLE as error:
        return None, f"Build run {run_id}'s {RECORD_ARTIFACT} cannot be read: {error}"


def review_conclusion(api: Api, repo: str, head: str, number: int) -> str:
    """The conclusion of the newest check run REVIEW_CHECK of the oss-verify App at the commit `head` for pull request
    `number` (its status while it has none), or NOT_REVIEWED when there is none. A check run whose external_id is not
    `number`, another pull request's at the same commit, is not counted. filter=all: GitHub's default, latest, can
    give only another pull request's newer check run, and this pull request's own would not be read."""
    found = [c for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/commits/{head}/check-runs?check_name={quote(REVIEW_CHECK)}"
                                     "&filter=all&per_page=100")
             for c in page.get("check_runs") or []
             if (c.get("app") or {}).get("id") == REVIEW_APP and c.get("external_id") == str(number)]
    if not found:
        return NOT_REVIEWED
    newest = max(found, key=lambda c: c["id"])
    return str(newest.get("conclusion") or newest.get("status"))


def size(value: object) -> bool:
    return value is None or (whole(value) and value >= 0)


def record_problem(record: object, sha: str) -> str:
    """Why the record cannot be used for the commit `sha`, or ''."""
    if not isinstance(record, dict) or record.get("schema") != RECORD_SCHEMA:
        return "the build record has another shape"
    pr, project = record.get("pr"), record.get("project")
    if not whole(pr) or pr < 1:
        return "the build record names no pull request"
    if not isinstance(project, str) or not NAME.fullmatch(project):
        return "the build record names no project"
    if record.get("sha") != sha:
        return f"the build record is of commit {record.get('sha')!r}, not {sha}"
    sizes = record.get("sizes")
    if not isinstance(sizes, dict) or not sizes:
        return "the build record lists no binary"
    for target, builds in sizes.items():
        if not isinstance(builds, dict) or "plain" not in builds:
            return f"the build record has no plain build of {target!r}"
        for value in builds.values():
            if not isinstance(value, dict) or set(value) != {"text", "exec"} or not all(map(size, value.values())):
                return f"the build record gives {target!r} a size that is not a byte count"
    return ""


def oversized(record: dict) -> list[str]:
    """Each plain binary whose size (the larger of .text and the executable segments) is above SIZE_LIMIT or
    unknown, as text for the reason line. A binary that the loader maps no executable byte of cannot run as built:
    its headers do not say its size, which is unknown."""
    out = []
    for target, builds in sorted(record["sizes"].items()):
        text, exe = builds["plain"]["text"], builds["plain"]["exec"]
        if text is None or exe is None or exe == 0:
            out.append(f"{target}.plain (size unknown)")
        elif max(text, exe) > SIZE_LIMIT:
            out.append(f"{target}.plain ({text:,} bytes of .text, {exe:,} executable bytes)")
    return out


def the_project(files: list[dict]) -> tuple[str | None, str]:
    """The one project a pull request's files change, or None and why not."""
    if len(files) >= MAX_LISTED_FILES:
        return None, f"it changes {len(files)} files or more, more than the API lists"
    names, kept = set(), False
    for f in files:
        for path in (f.get("filename"), f.get("previous_filename")):
            if path is None:
                continue
            parts = str(path).split("/")
            if len(parts) < 3 or parts[0] != "projects" or not NAME.fullmatch(parts[1]):
                return None, f"it changes {path!r}, which is not under one projects/<name>/"
            names.add(parts[1])
        kept |= f.get("status") != "removed"
    if len(names) != 1:
        return None, f"it changes {len(names)} projects, not one"
    if not kept:
        return None, "it removes its project"
    return names.pop(), ""


def open_at(pull: dict, repo: str, sha: str, head: tuple | None) -> str:
    """Why the pull request is not open, ready for review, into the default branch at `sha`, from `head` (repository,
    branch) when it is given, or ''."""
    base, at = pull.get("base") or {}, pull.get("head") or {}
    if pull.get("state") != "open":
        return f"it is {pull.get('state')}"
    if pull.get("draft") is not False:
        return "it is a draft: marking it ready for review builds it again, and that run decides"
    if base.get("ref") != DEFAULT_BRANCH or (base.get("repo") or {}).get("full_name") != repo:
        return f"it targets {base.get('ref')!r}, not {DEFAULT_BRANCH}"
    if at.get("sha") != sha:
        return f"its head is {at.get('sha')}, not {sha}: the run for its head decides"
    if head is not None and head_of_pull(pull) != head:
        return f"it comes from {at.get('label')!r}, not from the head the checks were run for"
    return ""


def project_yaml(api: Api, repo: str, project: str, sha: str) -> dict | None:
    """projects/<project>/project.yaml at `sha`, or None if it cannot be read."""
    try:
        data = api.raw(f"repos/{repo}/contents/projects/{project}/project.yaml?ref={sha}")
        if len(data) > MAX_PROJECT_YAML_BYTES:
            return None
        config = yaml.safe_load(data)
    except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, yaml.YAMLError, RecursionError):
        return None
    return config if isinstance(config, dict) else None


def language(config: dict | None) -> str | None:
    """The language project.yaml gives, lower case, or None."""
    value = (config or {}).get("language")
    return value.lower() if isinstance(value, str) else None


def standing(config: dict, login: str) -> str:
    """'' when triage.py's maintainer check passes for `login` on the repository `repo` names, else why not. It checks
    the pull request's author, not primary_contact. A repository not on github.com, a fork (whose owner is anyone who
    forked it), or a read that fails, does not pass."""
    match = triage.GITHUB_REPO.fullmatch(config.get("repo") or "") if isinstance(config.get("repo"), str) else None
    if not match:
        return "its repo is not a github.com repository, so the author's role there cannot be read"
    owner, name, _ = match.groups()
    try:
        gh = triage.GitHub(os.environ.get("GH_TOKEN"))
        meta = gh.find(f"repos/{triage.quote(owner, safe='')}/{triage.quote(name, safe='')}")
        if meta is None:
            return f"{owner}/{name} is not found on GitHub, or not public"
        if meta.get("fork") is not False:
            parent = (meta.get("parent") or {}).get("full_name") or "another repository"
            return f"{meta['full_name']} is a fork of {parent}, so owning it shows nothing"
        mark, evidence = triage.maintainer_row(gh, meta["full_name"], meta, login)
    except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - any failed read holds the enrollment for a person
        return f"the author's role on {owner}/{name} could not be read: {type(error).__name__}"
    if mark != triage.OK:
        return f"{login or 'the author'} is not shown to maintain {meta['full_name']}: {evidence}"
    return ""


def confirmed_by(api: Api, repo: str, number: int, pull: dict, author: str, since: str) -> str:
    """Who put CONFIRMED_LABEL on the pull request, when it carries it, that was someone other than its author, and it
    was put on after `since` (when the Build run of the head commit was created, so after that commit was pushed: a
    confirmation covers the commits it saw, not a later change of `repo`); else ''. Only an account with at least triage
    access to this repository can add a label (GitHub's permission model): a member of the organisation, or one of its
    Apps. The pull request's own author does not count."""
    if not labelled(pull, CONFIRMED_LABEL):
        return ""
    try:
        events = [e for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/issues/{number}/events?per_page=100") for e in page]
    except subprocess.CalledProcessError:
        return ""
    added = [e for e in events if e.get("event") == "labeled" and (e.get("label") or {}).get("name") == CONFIRMED_LABEL
             and isinstance(e.get("created_at"), str) and e["created_at"] > since]
    actor = ((added[-1].get("actor") or {}).get("login") or "") if added else ""
    return actor if actor and actor.lower() != author.lower() else ""


def label_for_a_person(where: str, lang: str, record: dict, number: int, project: str, sha: str) -> dict | None:
    """The label of the first thing a person decides by hand: a paused language, a name the statements repository
    cannot take, or a plain binary above SIZE_LIMIT (or of unknown size); else None."""
    if lang in PAUSED_LANGUAGES:
        return outcome("label", f"{where} is in {lang}, which is paused", number, project, sha, "language-paused")
    if not STATEMENTS_NAME.fullmatch(project):
        return outcome("label", f"{where}: the statements repository's project names have no dot", number, project,
                       sha, "name-review")
    over = oversized(record)
    if over:
        return outcome("label", f"{where} has a plain binary above {SIZE_LIMIT:,} bytes: {', '.join(over)}", number,
                       project, sha, "size-review")
    return None


def passes(result: dict) -> str:
    """'' when the run passes for REVIEW_PASSED, else why not: its decision is dispatch for an open pull request,
    which decision gives only when the newest REVIEW_CHECK check run of the commit is success (every check of review.md
    pass, or optional, as an optional fail of F5 or F8 is). decide_merged never asks it."""
    return "" if result["decision"] == "dispatch" else "the run sends nothing"


def trusted(api: Api, repo: str, login: str) -> bool | None:
    """review.yml's rule for trusted accounts (the bash function trusted of its route's trust step), with the same
    answers: True for an App of WRITER_BOTS, or an account that has write access (write_access); False for any other
    account, and for a login of another shape; None when it could not be read. WRITER_BOTS is read from the env of
    review.yml in this checkout, so that there is one list."""
    if not LOGIN.fullmatch(login):
        return False
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(CHECKOUT, REVIEW_WORKFLOW), encoding="utf-8") as file:
            bots = str(yaml.safe_load(file)["env"]["WRITER_BOTS"]).split(",")
    except (OSError, yaml.YAMLError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return None
    if login in bots:
        return True
    if login.endswith("[bot]"):
        return False
    return write_access(api, repo, login)


def steering_gate(api: Api, repo: str, number: int, pull: dict, files: list[dict], sha: str) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """The steering-file gate for pull request `number` (`pull`) at the commit `sha`, whose files are `files`: (why,
    approval). When no file (by its name or its previous name) is a steering file (steering.is_steering), both are ''.
    When one is, and a person approved `sha` (person_approval), why is '' and approval is the end of the reason that
    says who: " (<login> approved <sha7>, which changes the steering file <path>)". Else why says which file, and the
    run is none."""
    path = next((str(name) for f in files for name in (f.get("filename"), f.get("previous_filename"))
                 if name is not None and steering.is_steering(str(name))), None)
    if path is None:
        return "", ""
    login = person_approval(api, repo, number, pull, sha)
    if login is None:
        return f"changes the steering file {path}; no person's approval of {sha[:7]}", ""
    return "", f" ({login} approved {sha[:7]}, which changes the steering file {path})"


def labelled(pull: dict, name: str = REVIEW_PASSED) -> bool:
    """Whether the pull request carries the label `name`."""
    return name in {(label or {}).get("name") for label in pull.get("labels") or []}


def pull_of_head(api: Api, repo: str, sha: str, head: tuple) -> dict | None:
    """The pull request into the default branch from `head` (repository, branch) whose head commit is `sha`: an open
    one, else a closed one (merged or not), whose label a run takes off (review_passed); or None. It finds a fork's pull
    request too, which a workflow run does not name."""
    name, branch = head
    if not isinstance(name, str) or "/" not in name or not isinstance(branch, str):
        return None
    owner = urllib.parse.quote(name.split("/")[0], safe="")
    path = (f"repos/{repo}/pulls?state=all&base={DEFAULT_BRANCH}&head={owner}:{urllib.parse.quote(branch, safe='')}"
            "&per_page=100")
    closed = None
    for pull in (p for page in api.pages(path) for p in page):
        base, at = pull.get("base") or {}, pull.get("head") or {}
        if base.get("ref") == DEFAULT_BRANCH and (base.get("repo") or {}).get("full_name") == repo \
                and at.get("sha") == sha and head_of_pull(pull) == head:
            if pull.get("state") == "open":
                return pull
            if pull.get("state") == "closed" and closed is None:
                closed = pull
    return closed


def window_end(since: str) -> str:
    """The end of CONFIRMED_WINDOW after `since`, a time as GitHub gives it, in the same form."""
    return (datetime.datetime.strptime(since, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ") + CONFIRMED_WINDOW).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")




def label_heads(api: Api, repo: str, head: tuple, label: dict) -> set[str]:
    """The commits the pull request from `head` (repository, branch) may have been at when `label`, the newest labeled
    event of REVIEW_PASSED, was made, as the runs of CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW that the event may have started give them; an
    empty set when no such run is found, or the event names no account. The event's run is on pull_request (on
    pull_request_target before the move), from `head`, at the head of that moment, and its actor (its triggering actor
    too, but after a re-run by another account) is the account that put the label on. Each run of that account's of the
    workflow from `head` made in CONFIRMED_WINDOW after the event gives its commit: a run of another label that the
    account put on in that time (review.yml's held label, say) may be at another head, and is not told apart from the
    label's own here (older_than_head reads that label's event). One read lists the runs of both events."""
    actor = str((label.get("actor") or {}).get("login") or "").lower()
    if not actor or not isinstance(head[1], str):
        return set()
    since = label["created_at"]
    until = window_end(since)
    path = (f"repos/{repo}/actions/workflows/{os.path.basename(CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW)}/runs"
            f"?branch={urllib.parse.quote(head[1], safe='')}"
            f"&created={urllib.parse.quote(f'{since}..{until}', safe='')}&per_page=100")
    found = set()
    for run in (r for page in api.pages(path) for r in page.get("workflow_runs") or []):
        made, commit = time_of(run.get("created_at")), run.get("head_sha")
        logins = {str((run.get(key) or {}).get("login") or "").lower() for key in ("actor", "triggering_actor")}
        if run.get("path") == CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW and run.get("event") in PULL_EVENTS \
                and head_of(run) == head and made and since <= made <= until and actor in logins \
                and isinstance(commit, str) and SHA.fullmatch(commit):
            found.add(commit)
    return found


def older_than_head(api: Api, repo: str, sha: str, head: tuple, label: dict, events: list[dict]) -> tuple[bool, str]:
    """Whether the label whose newest labeled event is `label`, one of the pull request's `events`, is older than the
    run's head `sha`, from `head` (repository, branch), and how that is known, in words for the reason. The label is
    for a commit only when label_heads finds exactly one and `events` hold no other labeled event (of any label) by the
    same account made at or after `label` in CONFIRMED_WINDOW: then it is older exactly when that commit is not `sha`
    (a force push away from `sha` and back leaves a label put on for `sha`). When it finds none (the run was deleted or
    made late, or the event names no account), or more than one (the same account put a label on at another head in
    CONFIRMED_WINDOW), or when such another labeled event is found (the one run found may be that label's, at another
    head, with the label's own run missing), the head is not known, and the label is older: a true label may come off,
    and a false one never stays."""
    heads = label_heads(api, repo, head, label)
    workflow = os.path.basename(CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW)
    if not heads:
        return True, f"and no run of {workflow} that its labeled event started is found, so it counts as older than " \
                     f"{sha[:7]}"
    if len(heads) > 1:
        found = ", ".join(sorted(h[:7] for h in heads))
        return True, f"and its account's runs of {workflow} after it are at {found}, so its head is ambiguous and " \
                     f"it counts as older than {sha[:7]}"
    [commit] = heads
    actor, since = str((label.get("actor") or {}).get("login") or "").lower(), label["created_at"]
    until = window_end(since)
    others = [e for e in events if e is not label and e.get("event") == "labeled"
              and str((e.get("actor") or {}).get("login") or "").lower() == actor
              and since <= (time_of(e.get("created_at")) or "") <= until]
    if others:
        name = (others[0].get("label") or {}).get("name")
        return True, f"and its account put another label, {name!r:.60}, on at {others[0]['created_at']}, in the ten " \
                     f"minutes after it, so the one run of {workflow} found, at {commit[:7]}, may be that label's: " \
                     f"its head is ambiguous and it counts as older than {sha[:7]}"
    return commit != sha, f"for {commit[:7]}" + (f", not {sha[:7]}" if commit != sha else "")


def review_passed(api: Api, repo: str, result: dict, pull: dict | None = None, sha: str | None = None,
                  head: tuple | None = None, merged: bool = False) -> dict:
    """`result` with what happens to REVIEW_PASSED: review_passed (on, off, or '' for no change), review_passed_at
    (head for a change at a new head or a renewal, closed for a close or a merge, else ''), label_at (the time of the
    newest labeled event judged, for a change at a new head or a renewal), the pull request's number when it changes,
    and a clause of the reason that says why it changes or does not.

    The pull request is `pull`, the one the run read last; a run that is not of MERGED_WORKFLOW (`merged`) is about the
    commit `sha` from `head`, when it bound them, and when it read none, about the pull request into main from that
    head at that commit (pull_of_head: an open one, else a closed one). When that pull request is closed (merged or
    not) and carries the label, the run takes it off, whatever it decides and whatever its head, so that a later run
    takes off a label that a run of MERGED_WORKFLOW whose decision failed left. A run of MERGED_WORKFLOW changes
    nothing else, and never puts it on. When the pull request is not open at `sha` from `head`, the run for its head
    decides, and nothing changes. Else, when the label is off, a run that passes (passes) for an enrollment, whose
    files the decision dispatch has shown are under one projects/<name>/ and whose author is not trusted (trusted,
    with a clear answer), puts the label on, unless an account other than APP_LOGIN took it off before. When the label
    is on and older than the head (older_than_head: not shown to be for the head), a run that passes puts it on again,
    for the head, whoever the author is (the trust is not read): a renewal, which the workflow takes off before the
    send and puts on after it. Any other run takes it off; a label that is not older stays. When the pull request's
    events (or the runs that tell its age) cannot be read, nothing changes."""
    def say(clause: str, state: str = "", at: str = "", label_at: str = "", number: object = None) -> dict:
        out = dict(result, reason=" ".join(f"{result['reason']}; {REVIEW_PASSED} {clause}".split()))
        if state:
            out.update(pr=str(number), review_passed=state, review_passed_at=at, label_at=label_at)
        return out

    if not merged:
        if sha is None or head is None:
            return result   # the run binds no head
        if pull is None:
            try:
                pull = pull_of_head(api, repo, sha, head)
            except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, ValueError):
                return say(f"is left as it is: the pull request from that head at {sha[:7]} could not be read")
            if pull is None:
                return result
    number, on = pull.get("number"), labelled(pull)
    if pull.get("state") == "closed" and on and isinstance(number, int):
        return say(f"comes off: pull request {number} is closed", "off", "closed", number=number)
    if merged:
        return result
    if not isinstance(number, int) or pull.get("state") != "open" or (pull.get("head") or {}).get("sha") != sha \
            or head_of_pull(pull) != head:
        return say(f"is left as it is: the pull request is not open at {sha[:7]} from that head, and the run for its "
                   "head decides") if on else result
    author = str((pull.get("user") or {}).get("login") or "")
    if not on:
        if passes(result):
            return result
        # The trust read is made only here, where its answer decides something.
        trust = trusted(api, repo, author)
        if trust is True:
            return say(f"is not put on: its author {author} is trusted by review.yml's rule (write access, or an App "
                       "of WRITER_BOTS)")
        if trust is None:
            return say(f"is not put on: whether its author {author} is trusted could not be read")
    try:
        events = [e for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/issues/{number}/events?per_page=100") for e in page
                  if isinstance(e, dict)]
    except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, ValueError):
        return say("is left as it is: the pull request's events could not be read")
    if not on:
        removed = [e for e in events if e.get("event") == "unlabeled"
                   and (e.get("label") or {}).get("name") in REVIEW_PASSED_NAMES
                   and str((e.get("actor") or {}).get("login") or "").lower() != APP_LOGIN]
        if removed:
            remover = (removed[-1].get("actor") or {}).get("login") or "an account"
            return say(f"is not put on: {remover} took it off at {removed[-1].get('created_at')}, and the run does "
                       "not put it back")
        return say(f"goes on: {sha[:7]} is sent, its {REVIEW_CHECK} check run is success, and its author {author} is "
                   "not trusted", "on", number=number)
    labeled = sorted((e for e in events if e.get("event") == "labeled"
                      and (e.get("label") or {}).get("name") in REVIEW_PASSED_NAMES and time_of(e.get("created_at"))),
                     key=lambda e: e["created_at"])
    if not labeled:
        return say("is left as it is: no labeled event of it is found, so its age is not known")
    label_at = labeled[-1]["created_at"]
    try:
        older, how = older_than_head(api, repo, sha, head, labeled[-1], events)
    except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, ValueError):
        return say(f"is left as it is: the runs from that head could not be read, so whether its label of {label_at} "
                   f"is older than {sha[:7]} is not known")
    if not older:
        return say(f"stays: it was put on at {label_at} {how}")
    why = passes(result)
    if not why:
        return say(f"is put on again for {sha[:7]}, which is sent: it was put on at {label_at} {how}", "on", "head",
                   label_at, number)
    return say(f"comes off: it was put on at {label_at} {how}, and {why}", "off", "head", label_at, number)


def decide_merged(api: Api, repo: str, runs: Runs, run: dict) -> dict:
    """What a completed run of MERGED_WORKFLOW decides: dispatch, with merged=true, for the head commit of the pull
    request its title names, when that pull request is an enrollment merged into main whose required checks passed at
    that commit. The size line, a paused language and the name rule label as in decide; the review and the maintainer
    check are not asked, since the person who merged decided them. The pull request is read before the run's
    conclusion is: a close without a merge skips the run's job, and takes REVIEW_PASSED off (review_passed) as a merge
    does. A run on pull_request must be of the head of the pull request its title names, at its head commit or its
    merge commit, else it is none and changes no label."""
    run_id, event = run.get("id"), run.get("event")
    # pull_request runs the merge commit's copy of the file, which the pull request can change, so its title is bound
    # to its head below. pull_request_target ran the base branch's copy, whatever the pull request held (before the
    # move). A replay by hand must be main's.
    if event not in PULL_EVENTS and (event, head_of(run)) != ("workflow_dispatch", (repo, DEFAULT_BRANCH)):
        name, branch = head_of(run)
        return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} is neither a run of {MERGED_WORKFLOW} on pull_request or "
                       f"pull_request_target nor a replay of main's: it ran on {event} from {name}:{branch}")
    title = MERGED_TITLE.fullmatch(str(run.get("display_title") or ""))
    if title is None:
        return outcome("none", f"run {run_id}'s title {run.get('display_title')!r:.40} names no pull request")
    number = int(title.group(1))
    pull = api.get(f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{number}")
    commit, at = run.get("head_sha"), pull.get("head") or {}
    if event == "pull_request" and (head_of(run) != head_of_pull(pull) or not isinstance(commit, str)
                                    or not SHA.fullmatch(commit)
                                    or commit not in (at.get("sha"), pull.get("merge_commit_sha"))):
        name, branch = head_of(run)
        return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} ran from {name}:{branch} at {commit!r:.50}, which is not the head of "
                       f"pull request {number} at its head commit or its merge commit")
    return review_passed(api, repo, merged_decision(api, repo, runs, run, number, pull), pull, merged=True)


def merged_decision(api: Api, repo: str, runs: Runs, run: dict, number: int, pull: dict) -> dict:
    """decide_merged's decision for pull request `number`, as `pull` gives it."""
    run_id = run.get("id")
    if run.get("conclusion") != "success":
        return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} of {MERGED_WORKFLOW} is {run.get('conclusion')}, not success: its job "
                       "runs for a merge or a replay alone")
    replay = f"gh workflow run {os.path.basename(MERGED_WORKFLOW)} -f pr={number}"
    base = pull.get("base") or {}
    if pull.get("merged") is not True:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number} is not merged", number)
    if base.get("ref") != DEFAULT_BRANCH or (base.get("repo") or {}).get("full_name") != repo:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number} was merged into {base.get('ref')!r}, not {DEFAULT_BRANCH}",
                       number)
    sha, head = (pull.get("head") or {}).get("sha"), head_of_pull(pull)
    if not isinstance(sha, str) or not SHA.fullmatch(sha):
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}'s head {sha!r:.50} is not a commit id", number)
    files = [f for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{number}/files?per_page=100") for f in page]
    project, why = the_project(files)
    if project is None:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number} is not one enrollment: {why}", number, sha=sha)
    why, approval = steering_gate(api, repo, number, pull, files, sha)
    if why:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}: {why}", number, project, sha)
    # The runs the merge was made on: a run started by a later event decides nothing here (bound_checks).
    waiting, build_run = bound_checks(api, repo, sha, head, time_of(pull.get("merged_at")))
    waiting += pull_checks(api, repo, sha, number)
    if waiting:
        return outcome("none", f"required checks not passed at {sha[:7]}{approval}: {', '.join(waiting)}; once they "
                       f"pass, {replay} decides again", number, project, sha)
    record, why = build_record(api, repo, build_run)
    why = why or record_problem(record, sha)
    if not why and (record["pr"], record["project"]) != (number, project):
        why = f"the build record is of pull request {record['pr']} and projects/{record['project']}/"
    if why:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}{approval}: {why}", number, project, sha)
    where = f"pull request {number}: projects/{project}/ at {sha[:7]}{approval}"
    lang = language(project_yaml(api, repo, project, sha))
    if lang is None:
        return outcome("none", f"{where}: its project.yaml cannot be read for its language; {replay} decides again",
                       number, project, sha)
    label = label_for_a_person(where, lang, record, number, project, sha)
    if label:
        return label
    merged_by = (pull.get("merged_by") or {}).get("login") or "unknown"
    return dict(outcome("dispatch", f"pull request {number} was merged by {merged_by}{approval}: the merge decides the "
                        "review and the maintainer check", number, project, sha), merged="true")


def decide(api: Api, repo: str, run_id: int, run_event: str, head_sha: str) -> dict:
    """What the completed run decides (the module's header says how), with what happens to REVIEW_PASSED."""
    runs = Runs(api, repo)
    if run_event in PULL_EVENTS | {"workflow_dispatch"} \
            and runs.get(run_id).get("path") == MERGED_WORKFLOW:
        return decide_merged(api, repo, runs, runs.get(run_id))
    bound = {}
    result = decision(api, repo, runs, run_id, run_event, head_sha, bound)
    return review_passed(api, repo, result, **bound)


def decision(api: Api, repo: str, runs: Runs, run_id: int, run_event: str, head_sha: str, bound: dict) -> dict:
    """decide's decision for a run that is not a merge's. It puts in `bound` what review_passed needs, once it has
    read it: the commit and head the run is about (sha, head), and the pull request as it read it last (pull)."""
    if run_event in PULL_EVENTS:
        if not SHA.fullmatch(head_sha):
            return outcome("none", f"{head_sha!r} is not a commit id")
        trigger = runs.get(run_id)
        if trigger.get("head_sha") != head_sha:
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} is of {trigger.get('head_sha')}, not {head_sha}")
        sha, head = head_sha, head_of(trigger)
        bound.update(sha=sha, head=head)
        # Bound first: a run of a label other than CONFIRMED_LABEL, the first of a new head too, still takes off a label
        # older than that head (review_passed).
        if trigger.get("path") == CONFIRMED_WORKFLOW and trigger.get("conclusion") != "success":
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} is a label other than {CONFIRMED_LABEL}", sha=sha)
    elif run_event == "workflow_run":
        # A Review run after a run of Build or Triage. It runs on main: the run its title names gives the commit and
        # the head.
        run = runs.get(run_id)
        if (run.get("path"), run.get("event"), *head_of(run)) \
                != (REVIEW_WORKFLOW, "workflow_run", repo, DEFAULT_BRANCH):
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} is not a run of main's {REVIEW_WORKFLOW} on workflow_run")
        title = REVIEW_RUN_TITLE.fullmatch(str(run.get("display_title") or ""))
        if title is None:
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id}'s title {run.get('display_title')!r:.40} names no run")
        reviewed = runs.get(int(title.group(1)))
        sha, head = reviewed.get("head_sha"), head_of(reviewed)
        if (reviewed.get("path"), reviewed.get("event")) != (BUILD_WORKFLOW, "pull_request") \
                or not isinstance(sha, str) or not SHA.fullmatch(sha):
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id} reviewed run {title.group(1)}, which is not a run of "
                           f"{BUILD_WORKFLOW} on pull_request at a commit: only the review after a Build run decides")
        bound.update(sha=sha, head=head)
    elif run_event == "workflow_dispatch":
        # A Review run started by hand on main, for the pull request its title names.
        run = runs.get(run_id)
        if (run.get("path"), *head_of(run)) != (REVIEW_WORKFLOW, repo, DEFAULT_BRANCH):
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id}, started by hand, is not of {REVIEW_WORKFLOW} on {DEFAULT_BRANCH}")
        title = REVIEW_PULL_TITLE.fullmatch(str(run.get("display_title") or ""))
        if title is None:
            return outcome("none", f"run {run_id}'s title {run.get('display_title')!r:.40} names no pull request: a "
                           "review of an issue or a measurement sends nothing")
        pull = api.get(f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{title.group(1)}")
        sha, head = (pull.get("head") or {}).get("sha"), head_of_pull(pull)
        if not isinstance(sha, str) or not SHA.fullmatch(sha):
            return outcome("none", f"pull request {title.group(1)}'s head {sha!r:.50} is not a commit id")
        bound.update(sha=sha, head=head, pull=pull)
    else:
        return outcome("none", f"the run that completed was started by {run_event}, not by a pull request")
    waiting, build_run = bound_checks(api, repo, sha, head)
    if waiting:
        return outcome("none", f"required checks not passed at {sha[:7]}: {', '.join(waiting)}", sha=sha)
    record, why = build_record(api, repo, build_run)
    why = why or record_problem(record, sha)
    if why:
        return outcome("none", why, sha=sha)
    number, project = record["pr"], record["project"]
    bound["pull"] = api.get(f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{number}")
    why = open_at(bound["pull"], repo, sha, head)
    if why:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}: {why}", number, project, sha)
    files = [f for page in api.pages(f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{number}/files?per_page=100") for f in page]
    changed, why = the_project(files)
    if changed is None or changed != project:
        why = why or f"it changes projects/{changed}/, the record's project is {project}"
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number} is not one enrollment: {why}", number, project, sha)
    # The files were listed for whatever the head was when they were asked for: the head must still be `sha`.
    pull = bound["pull"] = api.get(f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{number}")
    why = open_at(pull, repo, sha, head)
    if why:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}: {why}", number, project, sha)
    waiting = pull_checks(api, repo, sha, number)
    if waiting:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}: required checks not passed at {sha[:7]}: "
                       f"{', '.join(waiting)}", number, project, sha)
    why, approval = steering_gate(api, repo, number, pull, files, sha)
    if why:
        return outcome("none", f"pull request {number}: {why}", number, project, sha)
    where = f"pull request {number}: projects/{project}/ at {sha[:7]}{approval}"
    config = project_yaml(api, repo, project, sha)
    lang = language(config)
    if lang is None:
        return outcome("none", f"{where}: its project.yaml cannot be read for its language; the next run decides",
                       number, project, sha)
    # Before the labels: a label that a person lifts by hand (size-review, say) must never be the only thing that
    # stands between a pull request whose review did not pass and its statements.
    conclusion = review_conclusion(api, repo, sha, number)
    if conclusion == NOT_REVIEWED:
        return outcome("none", f"{where}: {NOT_REVIEWED}: the oss-verify App wrote no {REVIEW_CHECK} check run on it",
                       number, project, sha)
    if conclusion != "success":
        return outcome("none", f"{where}: its newest {REVIEW_CHECK} check run is {conclusion}, not success", number,
                       project, sha)
    label = label_for_a_person(where, lang, record, number, project, sha)
    if label:
        return label
    author = (pull.get("user") or {}).get("login") or ""
    since = runs.get(build_run).get("created_at") if build_run is not None else None
    confirmed = confirmed_by(api, repo, number, pull, author, since) if isinstance(since, str) else ""
    why = "" if confirmed else standing(config, author)
    if why:
        return outcome("label", f"{where}: {why}", number, project, sha, "maintainer-review")
    return outcome("dispatch", f"{where} passed every required check, each plain binary has at most "
                   f"{SIZE_LIMIT:,} bytes of .text and of executable segments, and "
                   + (f"{confirmed} labelled it {CONFIRMED_LABEL}" if confirmed else "its author maintains its repository"),
                   number, project, sha)


def main() -> int:
    run_id = os.environ.get("RUN_ID", "")
    result = decide(Api(), os.environ["REPO"], int(run_id) if run_id.isdigit() else 0,
                    os.environ.get("RUN_EVENT", ""), os.environ.get("HEAD_SHA", ""))
    lines = "".join(f"{key}={value}\n" for key, value in result.items())
    path = os.environ.get("GITHUB_OUTPUT")
    if path:
        with open(path, "a", encoding="utf-8") as out:
            out.write(lines)
    sys.stdout.write(lines)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
